<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15966" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĕpĭnyctis</span></b> ,
			ĭdis, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπινυκτίς</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Night-blains</i>, <i>pustules that
				arise in the night</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 20, 2,
				6, § 12</span></i> (in <i><span class="en">Cels. 5,
				28, 15</span></i>, written as Greek).—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A kind of sore in the eyelid;</i> also called syce,
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				20, 6, 21, § 44</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
